Cicadian rhythms are internal timetables present in every single cell in every organ of our body, including the brain.

158
00:17:58,403 --> 00:18:05,043
And the circadian rhythms also constitute the master program that guides what time of the day or night

159
00:18:05,043 --> 00:18:10,624
every single gene of our 20,000 genes turn on or off.

160
00:18:11,403 --> 00:18:17,223
And thereby every single cell and all of our organs are at peak performance.

161
00:18:17,223 --> 00:18:26,104
In fact, these timely activities in our body help us to prevent disease, including to improve our immune function

162
00:18:26,104 --> 00:18:29,023
so that we can better fight infectious disease.

163
00:18:29,824 --> 00:18:35,364
They also accelerate repair mechanisms so that we can recover faster from injuries.

164
00:18:36,104 --> 00:18:41,443
They also optimize our brain function to improve our emotional and intellectual health.

165
00:18:41,443 --> 00:18:50,483
This circadian rhythm also supercharge our metabolism, detoxification and DNA repair mechanisms so that we live at a very low risk for chronic diseases.

166
00:18:51,243 --> 00:18:57,324
But you might wonder, well, if it is already encoded in our DNA, why aren't we living already a healthy life?

167
00:18:58,163 --> 00:19:03,063
The reason may be we are living out of alignment with our circadian rhythm.

168
00:19:03,063 --> 00:19:05,183
Think of it like this.

169
00:19:05,584 --> 00:19:13,503
Just like our body runs on 20,000 genes, a typical car runs on 20,000 parts, down to the last screw.

170
00:19:14,023 --> 00:19:24,104
But a car today can run perfectly fine for more than 200,000 miles if we take good care of it and follow a few simple safe driving rules.

171
00:19:24,104 --> 00:19:34,084
So similarly, I hope I can share six simple rules with you to take care of your circadian car and drive it for very long life.

172
00:19:34,824 --> 00:19:37,884
So the rule number one is eight hours in bed.

173
00:19:38,223 --> 00:19:45,723
Try to go to bed at consistent time and be in bed for eight hours so that you can get at least seven hours of restorative sleep.

174
00:19:46,203 --> 00:19:53,364
During sleep, our circadian clocks produce hormones and chemicals to repair and rejuvenate our brain and body.

175
00:19:53,364 --> 00:19:58,243
Then rule number two is to avoid eating for at least an hour in the morning.

176
00:19:58,943 --> 00:20:08,663
After we get up, our organs take at least an hour to fully be awake because that's the time when our night hormones go down and our day hormones go up.

177
00:20:09,183 --> 00:20:12,644
And our body is not fully prepared to properly digest food.

178
00:20:13,203 --> 00:20:20,644
So by avoiding food for at least an hour, we can improve digestion and also we can have a better control over our blood glucose.

179
00:20:20,644 --> 00:20:25,203
Then rule number three is time-restricted eating or intermittent fasting.

180
00:20:25,523 --> 00:20:26,943
This is the most important.

181
00:20:27,063 --> 00:20:28,943
This is the core of circadian optimization.

182
00:20:29,443 --> 00:20:37,084
And I'm proud that my research team at the Salk Institute almost 10 years ago discovered this revolutionary idea.

183
00:20:37,084 --> 00:20:47,124
So try to eat your breakfast at a consistent time every day because breakfast synchronizes all circadian rhythms in most of our organs.

184
00:20:47,963 --> 00:20:57,503
Starting from breakfast, eat all of your meals and beverages of the day within the next eight, nine, ten or maximum 12 hours.

185
00:20:57,503 --> 00:21:08,604
This pattern of eating within a consistent time and living somewhere between 12 to 16 hours of fasting is called time-restricted eating or now popular as intermittent fasting.

186
00:21:09,104 --> 00:21:14,243
This is your best way to maintain a robust circadian rhythm.

187
00:21:14,243 --> 00:21:24,804
And this helps in multiple ways to have a better handle on your weight, blood pressure, blood glucose, immune system and many more.

188
00:21:25,384 --> 00:21:28,144
Number four is get 30 minutes of daylight.

189
00:21:28,483 --> 00:21:32,523
Another major breakthrough from my lab is about daylight.

190
00:21:32,983 --> 00:21:35,844
So step outdoors to get 30 minutes of daylight.

191
00:21:35,844 --> 00:21:46,243
Because even on a cloudy day, staying outdoor for 30 to 60 minutes is the best way to resynchronize our brain clock.

192
00:21:46,563 --> 00:21:47,644
This is the brain booster.

